A||N||7||rockcrawl||Need shift kit for 4spd auto||||7||
Z||000000||rockcrawl||11-07-2000||09:46 PM||||I'm finally replacing the 2.8 in my 87 GT, and while I'm at it, I'm putting in a TH440T4/4T60 four speed auto. I've been looking for a shift improver kit for it, but having no luck finding one. Anyone know who makes one? If not, I'll just play around with the governor springs and set the throttle valve cable really tight. I'd love to be able to chirp the tires when it shifts.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT (awaiting new engine)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<P>"Confidence is the feeling you have before you fully understand the situation"||||reg||7
Z||000001||87GTZ34||11-08-2000||01:43 AM||||I'm not sure, but I think the clutch/seal sizes from longitudinal trans fit corresponding transaxles. Check the B&M page <A HREF="http://www.bmracing.com/bmframe.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.bmracing.com/bmframe.htm</A>  and give them a call.  If I get time tomorrow I'll do the same as I have the E version that needs to be stiffened up.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||PTW87GT||11-08-2000||07:10 AM||||Rockcrawl,<BR>I am buying the same transaxle, how difficult was it to install?  Are the keeping the 2.8/3.1 block.  My trans comes with a 3800 (Series 1)||||reg||1
Z||000003||elfiero||11-08-2000||09:26 AM||||rockcrawl,I put my 440T4 in w/o modifying<BR>anything and after about half a dozen hard<BR>launches,I toasted third gear!I found another<BR>trans out of a 3800S/C and I talked to my<BR>local trans guru.He says there is no shift<BR>kit available per se,but he can raise the<BR>line pressure and tighten the governor springs which will firm up the shifts.BTW,<BR>I'm using a TPIv8-awsome burnouts,unreal<BR>midrange,aint no ricers got sh*t on me!||||reg||6
Z||000004||rockcrawl||11-08-2000||04:26 PM||||87GTZ34, I was also thinking that the internals are similar to one of the longitudinal transmisions, but I don't want to do any guess work. <P>PTW87GT, My trans also came with a 3800. I used the 3800 with a 4spd Muncie in another car. The current project car is getting a stock rebuilt 2.8 with the 4 spd auto. It will be going together tonight, I'll let you know how it goes, but it seems pretty straightforward. The trans is about 2" longer on the passenger side, so it will require a shorter axle, drivers side is close enough to use the stock axle. There are lots of posts about this in the archives.<P>elfiero, I'd say you overpowered that poor trans! Anyway, mine should be fine with the wimpy 2.8, I just didn't want it to shift like an Oldsmobile. I'll experiment with the governor springs and TV cable, but that's about the extent of my tinkering without knowing what the hell I'm doing.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT (awaiting new engine)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<P>"Confidence is the feeling you have before you fully understand the situation"||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||11-08-2000||07:14 PM||||<A HREF="http://www.txchange.com/" TARGET=_blank>Transmission Exchange Co.</A> has TransGo kits for nearly anything made. Has anyother parts you may need while it's appart.||||reg||1
Z||000006||87GTZ34||11-09-2000||12:09 AM||||I called B&M today.  They told me there's nothing for transaxles and they are totally different than the longitudinals.  He was pretty negative & hopeless so being the doubting Thomas that I am, I will investigate more.  I can't believe the 'parts is parts' GM engineers reinvented the wheel for transaxles...||||reg||1
